{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T20:58:15.023Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"1cfc0cbf75050fc488823206","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T20:58:15.023Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:15.019Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Contract check: upstream issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1549 separates mutation-lease fencing from already-completed dead-owner recovery. The published SDK source returns from cleanup-gate recovery while the gate age is at most 10000 ms, before inspecting its recorded owner. Thus a provably killed fence owner still blocks the default 3000 ms acquisition, as the minimal reproduction shows. This supports treating the recovery delay as an SDK regression rather than adding a package retry layer. The original issue concerns preventing stale overwrite; this follow-up concerns crash recovery after that fix."}]}],"before_hash":"fe081cd50c31762722ecf994692b2126c69c07096e30fe2d1f8f6fb5ce6735fc","after_hash":"6f0b5d39a63a84fa3c20c4eff8b172c75d7e520d2ca6599c483723caeb9bba37","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fb4c802b0ded44a97365c3cbdfe67991fbb83c04fe56936d4a8b6cabfa5f6002"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T22:08:18.501Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"1cfc0cbf75050fc488823206","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-26T22:08:18.501Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Exact pushed commit 5dd620a08ddf93ccf2a13047340932459ddf0fc4 reproduces the upstream recovery failure in Node 26 CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40408966320/job/121874051444 . The root-write SIGKILL test reports lock_conflict with reason lock_owner_dead, waited_ms 3013, owner_handoffs 0, while raw four-metric coverage remains 100%. This confirms the SDK-only fence plus SIGKILL reproduction already recorded on pm-rlm-tc1023. Regenerated changelog is preserved and production ledger source remains identical to the dependency bump. This PR remains blocked on upstream default-wait dead-owner recovery; do not add package retries, extend waits, skip the crash test or lower thresholds."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T22:08:18.501Z"}],"before_hash":"6f0b5d39a63a84fa3c20c4eff8b172c75d7e520d2ca6599c483723caeb9bba37","after_hash":"78c26102bcd3475f4e079f9040f46128c6be0b0240e007577713b1c80ba066aa","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4e6c2b28c6784c52d5fb5d02b9e4c82ed9550d89c11f0101535dc3255248e4b1"}
